during the Revolutionary War the Second  Continental Congress drafted the  Articles of Confederation which was  ratified in 1781 the Articles of  Confederation did not give the federal  government enough power this caused some  problems for the new federal government  like the inability to levy taxes or  enforce laws in 1787 Madison and  Hamilton convinced the delegates to the  Constitutional Convention scrapped the  Articles of Confederation and draft a  new constitution that would give more  power to the federal government and  strengthen the bonds between states  anti-federalists like Patrick Henry Sam  Adams and James Monroe object they  believed that the Constitution gave too  much power to the federal government and  demanded that a Bill of Rights be added  the convention with the notable  exceptions of Edmund Randolph Elvidge  Gary and George Mason approved the  Constitution and it was ratified by the  states in 1788 in 1789  James Madison submitted a series of 39  amendments to the Constitution Congress  passed 12 and the states ratified 10 the  10 amendments now known as the Bill of  Rights were ratified in 1791  you
 

